# Project architecture

Riddlr is a local-first, read-only intelligence engine. The core is asset-class
agnostic. Crypto and Equities are supported market domains. Forex, Commodities,
and Macro are coming soon.

## Data path

Source → Evidence → Entity/Asset/Instrument → Event → domain context → Analysis →
Validated signal → dashboard / notification policy.

## Layout

- `apps/web` Vite React SPA
- `apps/server` Fastify API and BullMQ worker entrypoints
- `packages/domain` generic contracts
- `packages/domain-crypto` Crypto domain module
- `packages/domain-equities` Equities domain module
- `packages/crypto` cryptography only (AES, Argon2id, TOTP)
- PostgreSQL is source of truth; Valkey is not

## Forbidden

- Next.js, Prisma, trading, private keys, scraping Discord/X
- Importing `@riddlr/domain-crypto` or `@riddlr/domain-equities` from generic engine packages
- Fake signals, fake metrics, or executable coming-soon domains
- Committing `initial-prompt.md`, `system-prompt.md`, secrets, or transcripts
- Onboarding longer than four steps
